61,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Based on our discussion, Candidate C is the only logical choice. It leverages our spare maintenance capacity and avoids the staffing shortages and structural risks we identified. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for Candidate C. It's the best way to tackle those connection delays without getting stuck in the mid-city traffic or staffing messes. Candidate C it is!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Given the ring-fenced construction funds and the operational capacity for lift maintenance, Candidate C is the only fiscally responsible choice. It avoids the pitfalls of our trimmed operating budget. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"My heart is at peace with this decision. History has shown us that these upgrades are achievable, and our current capacity supports them. I cast my vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Candidate C avoids the data conflicts of the fare platform and the structural hazards of the pre-war shells. It is the most reliable path forward. I vote for Candidate C.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Since everyone has already cast their vote for Candidate C and we are in complete agreement, there is no need for further deliberation. I am satisfied with this outcome.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
